# Secrets — real logins live in .env, never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Your real environments (seeded from config/urls.example.json on first run).
# Keeps your live URLs out of the open-source repo.
config/urls.json

# Role definitions (seeded from config/roles.example.json + your .env on first
# run). Local per checkout; holds no secrets but stays out of the shared repo.
config/roles.json

# Saved site groups (named env presets). Local per checkout; no secrets.
config/groups.json

# App-managed test metadata (group/priority/owner/notes). A committed seed ships
# the "Examples" group so a fresh clone has a populated Tests page; the app may
# add/edit entries locally on top of it.

# Internal planning notes — kept locally, not part of the open-source repo.
GRAIN-PLAN.md

# Company-specific working docs (deployment pitches, tenant details, host names, real env names).
# This repo is PUBLIC and ships generic by design (CLAUDE.md "Open source, stays generic"), so
# anything naming a real company, tenant or host uses this suffix and stays out of git.
*.local.md

# Runtime SQLite db (data/greenroom.db + WAL/SHM). Shared runtime state, never committed.
/data/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Lockfiles stay ignored — but NOT for the old reason. The original note here said bun could not
# resolve a depth-2+ nested github git-dep graph (greenroom -> pantry -> 4 layers) so a lock could
# never be regenerated. That blocker is GONE: @tjakoen/pantry was removed, the whole shared layer
# is on public npmjs, and both `bun install` (82 pkgs) and `npm install` (83 pkgs) now resolve from
# scratch against an empty HOME with no credentials. So a committed lock IS regenerable now, and
# committing one would be a reasonable call for reproducibility — it is simply not the current
# policy. Decide deliberately before changing it; do not "restore" it on the strength of the
# stale reasoning that used to live here (audit 2026-08-03).
bun.lock
package-lock.json

# Playwright output. Anchored to the repo root (leading /) so these DON'T also
# match the committed demo/ fixtures (demo/test-results, demo/runs, …).
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/

# Local run history (archived reports, stays on this machine)
/runs/

# graphify's generated code+doc graph — regenerable, host-local
graphify-out/

# Editor-host scratch state. `.nimbalyst/transcript-images/` collects UI screenshots the
# assistant captures while working — including captures of the PLATFORM edition showing real
# account emails and internal environment names. Seventeen of them were committed by a
# `git add .` in "Ready Greenroom for Use" (audit 2026-08-03); they never reached a remote,
# but nothing stopped it happening. This rule is that stop. Never un-ignore it.
.nimbalyst/

# Per-machine Claude Code settings (permission grants accreted while working,
# absolute paths, personal hooks). The committed .claude/settings.json keeps only
# the handful of rules that make sense for anyone working on this repo.
.claude/settings.local.json
